</div></section>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="representative-checks"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Open representative content</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Choose examples that give you a useful spread rather than checking only the newest item. Open an older photo and a recent photo. Inspect a contact detail and a calendar entry. Review a message and open a sample local file or download. For an important app, check its actual records or account content rather than the presence of its icon.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Cloud content may still be downloading or synchronising. A restored layout is not proof that every item is available. The <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/108770">Apple explanation of iCloud synchronisation and backup</a> is a useful reminder to check synchronised content separately.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Record observations in plain language. For example, “recent photo opened; older folder still pending” is more useful than “transfer successful”. Keep the source device available while any important result is uncertain.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "One app icon proves very little") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">An icon does not prove that the app’s records, downloads, messages, purchases or account session copied across.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="access-and-settings"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Review access and device settings</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Confirm that the destination unlocks normally and that the relevant backup and find-device settings are understood. Use the official device instructions for the exact model and software version. Only change settings you understand, and do not assume that a recovery prompt means recovery is complete.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Authenticator apps and app-specific account access may need a vendor process. Retain the old device until those checks are resolved. Mobile-service activation, SIM or eSIM changes and porting belong to the mobile provider. Wi-Fi and internet access do not prove that mobile calling or SMS is ready.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If you perform an ordinary test of calling or messaging, keep it limited and never use an emergency number as a test. Banking and myGov setup or recovery remain separate official-provider processes and are not part of a standard transfer check.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "Provider access is a separate job") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Do not treat a successful Wi-Fi connection, copied app or unlocked screen as proof that mobile service, authenticator access, banking or myGov recovery is ready.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="pending-work"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Record observations and next owners</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Use a short pending list to separate what you observed from what still needs action. The example below is fictional and does not represent a completed transfer.</p><div class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto" role="region" aria-label="New device checks reference" tabindex="0"><table role="table" class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm md:text-base"><thead><tr><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Item</th><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Observation</th><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Next owner</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Item" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Photos</td><td data-label="Observation" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Recent photo opened; older album still pending</td><td data-label="Next owner" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Device owner to check sync status</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Item" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Authenticator</td><td data-label="Observation" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">App installed; sign-in not verified</td><td data-label="Next owner" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">App provider process</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Item" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Mobile service</td><td data-label="Observation" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Wi-Fi works; mobile calling not tested</td><td data-label="Next owner" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Mobile provider and device owner</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Do not erase, reset, trade in or discard the source because this list is complete. A representative check cannot guarantee that every record transferred. Resolve important pending items first and keep the source unerased until you have made a separate, informed decision.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "A checklist is not an erase approval") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Completion means the listed checks were recorded. It does not authorise erasing the source or prove that all content and account access are present.</p>{% endcall %}
